# pnpm's default (isolated) layout: every dependency under node_modules/.pnpm, symlinked into the
# workspace that names it. `pnpm deploy --legacy` in the Dockerfiles works under it.

# The published Beacon packages (@beaconsgg/*) come from the public npm registry: the wire
# contract and primitives the server is built on, and the build, test, lint and format presets.
# An install needs no token. A token is needed only to publish, and it never goes in this file:
# pnpm drops this whole file when a ${VAR} in it is unset. The release workflow writes it to the
# runner's user config from the NPM_TOKEN repository secret.
